{"summary":"Both amendments identify real defects: the TUI test is now selecting the wrong action because it is index-coupled to a reordered list, and the save migration silently changes legacy `TrimPlants` behavior from in-tank detritus routing to biomass export.","votes":[{"amendment_id":"fr-2-5f3aaec6","decision":"accept","rationale":"Accept. The current test fails exactly for the stated reason: after `TrimPlantsAndLeaveCuttings` was inserted into `ActionKind::ALL`, advancing 5 times lands on `CleanFilter` rather than `AddShrimp`, so the test no longer exercises integer-only validation and can succeed incorrectly. Updating the navigation, preferably by selecting `ActionKind::AddShrimp` directly instead of depending on positional order, restores the intended coverage and removes brittle coupling to enum ordering."},{"amendment_id":"fr-2-d613a3c7","decision":"accept","rationale":"Accept. The migration currently rewrites legacy `TrimPlants` to `TrimPlantsAndRemove`, but repository history shows the old `TrimPlants` implementation reduced plant biomass and routed the trimmed mass into `fine_detritus`, which matches the new `TrimPlantsAndLeaveCuttings` semantics rather than the remove/export variant. That means loading a schema-4 save with queued trim actions now changes gameplay behavior silently, which is a real save-compatibility bug unless it is explicitly documented as an intentional semantic break."}]}